A||||5||84 2in1||Turbo chargeing a 2.5||||1||
Z||000000||84 2in1||05-30-2001||07:23 PM||||are there any sites on how to do this conversion useing a 2.2 dodge turbo?-B-||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||05-30-2001||07:32 PM||||Yep!  It's a really simple process<P>1)  Remove engine<BR>2)  Buy 2.8 V-6 Engine<BR>3)  Install Design One Kit on engine<BR>4)  Install Engine in car.<P><BR>Just me, that's what I would do.  BUT I have a feeling that fabricating a turbo onto a 2.5 would probably be easier than custom designing one for the 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||05-30-2001||07:46 PM||||Yes, it's in here somewhere. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||05-30-2001||09:09 PM||||Fiero Conversions Inc in Canada does sell a<BR>turbo for the Duke BTW.<BR>Ph.# (519)-972-4989<P>I've never seen any conversion for the 2.2 dodge though. I've heard of some of the Fiat guys doing that conversion but not in a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||BV MotorSports||05-30-2001||09:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84 2in1:<BR><B>are there any sites on how to do this conversion useing a 2.2 dodge turbo?-B-</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I owned a turbocharged 2.5 4 cyl fiero. So I may be of some help.<P>First thing is that you are going to need an exhaust manifold. If you are VERY lucky you could call and ask Jim Sutter (IRM) if he could look and see if he has enuff spare parts left over to supply you with most of the "big" items for the 4cyl turbo kit. Good luck though I couldnt get him to get off his ass.<P>If not you could have a turbo manifold made but it wont be cheap. After that pick a turbo. A 12a Mitsubishi would be a good choice. Its rated at 365cfm @ 15psi of boost (about 6 on a fiero w/o intercooler max!) <BR>This turbo is found on the 85.5-89 Mitsubishi Starion/ Chrysler Conquest.<P>A "hat" would be needed for the t/b on the fiero. A paxton or procharger carb hat may work with or with out mods.<P>Plumbing, Could get it mocked up and take it to a GOOD muffler shop to bend up some stainless for the intake and exhaust.<P>Need to tie into the oil system for oil...most put in a T at the oil sending unit.<P>Coolant lines will have to be made if you run a Mitsu turbo since they are both oil and coolant cooled. (better turbos are)<P>Need an oil cooler. Some say you dont need it if you oil temp stays below 260deg but why take a chance. <P>Oil return line has to be 3x as big as the oil feed line to ensure proper oil return (oil looks like whipped cream after the turbo)and has to be able to gravity drain. Tap into the oil pan ABOVE the oil level approx 1inch or more to ensure proper drain back.<P>An MSD boost timing master will help with the ignition and you may need a rising rate fuel pressure regulator to increase fuel pressure at the injectors. <P>An AIR FUEL meter is a MUST!!!!! I have seen them from as cheap as $30 to $400 bucks. That is still cheaper than a new engine.<P>If you want to run over 6psi an intercooler of say a turbo daytona (nice I/C and compact)<BR>would alow you to run about 10-12 psi. <BR>Im not saying for sure you can run that much boost so dont even try without atlest verifying fuel press and a/f ratio. An EGT guage is way better than an A/F guage, so thats something to consider.<P>If you are serious go to the local branes and noble etc and pick up a book called turbochargers by hugh maclnnes (part of the HP Books series)<P>see a turbo 4cyl @ <A HREF="http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1" TARGET=_blank>http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1</A> <P>look for the turbo 4cyl fiero link. If you have anymore questions feel free to contact me.<P>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000005||SPDFREK||05-31-2001||01:01 AM||||OK, I cheated, I bought mine with the turbo in it. however, the guy gave me the sales slips for everything!(very nice of him I think) anyway, he got the motor/tranny out of a 1990 Sunbird GT in a local salvage yard.<BR>(2.0L turbo) it is somewhere around 175HP stock he told me, and he said he didn't have to do to many mods. how true that is I don't know I just know that the cars runs a LOT better then my friends non turbo Duke. PS, I also have sales slips for the wiring harness and brain, I don't know if those are what's in it, but I would guess it is.<P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||4
